  project: Pricing v2
  owner: Marta
  status: In review

# Moving to usage-based pricing

Seat pricing punishes the teams who adopt us fastest. Every person they add costs them money, so they stop adding people, and the workspace we want them to live in becomes the one they ration. Four of five interviews said a version of this without being asked.

@note ask Ana before Friday

## What we heard

@quote by="User P7" source="Discovery interview 3"
  We stopped adding people to the workspace because every new seat cost money. That is exactly backwards from what you want us doing.

## The decision

@decision title="Usage-based, billed monthly, with a floor" status=accepted date=2026-09-19
  context: Seat pricing punishes the teams who adopt fastest
  choice: Usage-based with a floor, so revenue stays predictable
  consequences: Revenue is lumpier and forecasting needs rework

@metric name="Weekly active teams" value="1,240" target="2,000" trend=up status=on-track
  Growing 8% week-over-week since the playground shipped.

## What could go wrong

@risk level=high title="Churn among small teams"
  Small teams pay less under usage pricing, and they are also the loudest segment and the first to post about a change.
  mitigation: Grandfather existing plans for 12 months.

@warn
  Finance needs 30 days' notice before any billing change ships.

@assumption title="Teams will accept a floor" confidence=medium
  Teams tolerate a minimum charge when it is visibly lower than the bill they pay today.
  validation: Offer it to 5 accounts at renewal. Three of five accept without escalating.
